# ReferenceCombobox for Données de référence

Any form field whose options come from **Données de référence** MUST use `ReferenceCombobox` — never a raw `Select`, `EquipmentSearchSelect`, or ad-hoc lookup.

Governance philosophy: `docs/engineering/REFERENCE_GOVERNANCE.md`  
Backend SSOT: `src-tauri/src/reference/governance.rs` (`ACTIVE_ENFORCEMENT_PHASE = Target`)  
Combobox guide: `docs/engineering/REFERENCE_COMBOBOX.md`  
Implementation plan: `docs/engineering/REFERENCE_GOVERNANCE_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`

## Categories (exactly one per domain)

| Category | Meaning | Combobox create |
|----------|---------|-----------------|
| **A** System Catalog | Product-owned, read-only | Never |
| **B** Operational Dictionary | Tenant live CRUD | Yes when `can_operational_create` + `ref.manage` |
| **C** Controlled Business Catalog | Draft → publish | Never (no silent live write) |

## Required path

1. Assign domain to A, B, or C per `REFERENCE_GOVERNANCE.md`
2. Register `referenceType` in `src/components/reference/reference-types.ts` (labels only — **no** create flags)
3. Drop in `<ReferenceCombobox referenceType="…" value={…} onChange={…} />`
4. Create-from-dropdown only when governance capabilities allow it (Category B)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Select value={familyCode} onValueChange={setFamilyCode}>…</Select>

// ✅ GOOD (B domain)
<ReferenceCombobox
  referenceType="equipment.family"
  value={familyCode}
  onChange={setFamilyCode}
  parentCode={classCode}
/>
```

## Hard rules

- Never offer a mutate action the backend will reject for that category.
- Manager and Combobox must follow the same capability snapshot.
- Labels: **label only**; form value may be **code** or **id** (`valueMode`).
- Do not reintroduce `allowOperationalCreate` or registry permission booleans.
- Do not grow `lookup_*` for new reference fields.
- Create CTA gated by capabilities + `ref.manage`.
- Export is view-only (`ref.view`); do not invent export capability flags.
